  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.2.0 — Re-enable buffer ring + SQPOLL mode\n• Re-enable provided buffer ring (multishot recv) — stalling bug fixed\n  on kernel 6.6+. Eliminates per-recv Pin()/Dispose() overhead.\n  Controlled via EnableBufferRing option (default: true).\n• Add SQPOLL mode support (EnableSqPoll option). Kernel polls the SQ ring,\n  eliminating io_uring_enter syscalls. Requires CAP_SYS_NICE or root.\n• Ring constructor now accepts setup flags for SQPOLL and future kernel features.\n• BufferRingSize option for tuning buffer ring depth (default: 256).\n\nv1.1.0 — Performance: lock-free send path\n• Send operations are now enqueued to the IO loop via ConcurrentQueue + eventfd\n  instead of acquiring SubmitLock per send. Eliminates 90K+/s lock contentions\n  on multi-core machines.\n• IO loop is now the sole SQ producer — all submissions are batched into a\n  single io_uring_enter per loop iteration.\n• Reduces per-send syscalls from 1 each to 0 (batched with recv/accept work).\n\nv1.0.1 — Bug fix\n• Fix IOSQE_BUFFER_SELECT constant: was 1<<3 (0x08), now 1<<5 (0x20)\n  Matches kernel definition. Fixes EFAULT when using buffer rings with recv.\n• Add test project with 10 tests (unit + integration)\n• Add InternalsVisibleTo for test project\n\nv1.0.0 — Initial release\n• Drop-in io_uring transport via UseIoUring()\n• Multishot recv with buffer rings\n• Zero-copy send (SEND_ZC)\n• Registered file descriptors\n• Targets net8.0, net9.0, net10.0",
